            "review_text": "ozvpm_andy\nAdelaide, Australia765 contributions\n0\nA disappointing experience\nMar 2019 • Couples\nOK - so first of all, the food we ordered was good - but the overall dining experience was sub standard. Believe me, we are not fussy diners, but this was all quite bizarre!\n\nWe arrived early to avoid the peak and ordered 2 appetisers, some rice and two mains. The waitress didn't bother to write anything down and wandered off to the kitchen. After a few minutes our first starter arrived - tasty spring rolls, but no sauce of any kind with them. As we finished those, my chicken main arrived - no rice, just the main, and then just as we were finishing that, the second main arrived, again no rice in sight.\n\nWe waited for the rice, which we were sure they had forgotten, but it didn't arrive, until eventually I gained the attention of the other waitress, who brought the rice once we had about one mouthful of beef left to eat.\n\nOnce again, our second appetiser had still not arrived, and we were about to ask for the bill (assuming it had been forgotten), when suddenly, our onion rings (again with no sauce) arrived!!!\n\nWow!\n\nI went to the counter to pay and was asked to go and sit down and they would bring the bill - which they also promptly forgot to bring, and it only arrived after another 15 wait and a reminder to staff.\n\nSo - great food but a terrible dining experience.\n\nThank goodness we didn't visit when it was busy!!!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten March 16, 2019",
